{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a metallaphotoredox-catalyzed three-component 1,2-carboallylation of terminal alkynes using allylic carbonates and alkyl trifluoroborates. The reaction utilizes a dual catalytic system of 4CzIPN (organic photocatalyst) and a nickel catalyst. A key feature is the use of pyrene as a triplet energy transfer (EnT) modulator to achieve stereodivergent access to both (E,Z)- and (Z,Z)-1,4-dienes from the same starting materials.",
